+# apps/web — agent instructions
+
+Rules for the customer-facing web app in `apps/web/`.
+
+## 1. Setup
+
+- Install packages with pnpm only; npm and yarn are not allowed in this app.
+- Copy `.env.example` to `.env.local` before running the dev server.
+
+## 2. Code layout
+
+- The old onboarding guide said to put page components under `pages/`, but in fact routes live in `src/app/`.
+- Name component files in PascalCase (`ProductCard.tsx`).
+- Follow the naming rules in `docs/web-conventions.md`.
+
+## 3. Data and state
+
+- We used to fetch data with SWR inside each component, but after the 2026-03 migration every request now goes through `src/api/client.ts`.
+- Do not call `fetch` directly — the API client attaches the auth header and refreshes an expired token, and a direct call logs the user out when the token expires.
+- Client state uses Redux Toolkit ([ADR-0012](../../docs/adr/0012-client-state-redux.md)).
+
+## 4. Styling
+
+- Do not add a CSS-in-JS library — ADR-0009 rejected it because of its runtime cost on low-end phones.
+- Use `next/image` for every image.
+- Exception: pages under `src/app/(marketing)/` may use plain `<img>` tags, because the marketing CDN resizes those images itself.
+
+> TODO: add before/after screenshots for the styling rules above.
+
+## 5. Testing
+
+- Our unit tests started as a hackathon project in 2025. The team found that slow, flaky snapshot tests were holding everyone up, and after several retrospectives we agreed to keep the suite small and fast; today it runs in under a minute on a laptop. So, run `pnpm test` before every commit.
+- Run `pnpm test:e2e` locally before every push.
+
+## 6. CI and review
+
+- Do not run e2e tests locally; CI runs them on every PR.
+- Open PRs against `main`; one approval from the web team is required.
